---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: Pull requests fix themselves
    accDescr: A check fails. Where a command fixes what it found, such as the format of the code, the whitespace of a text file or the rules of markdownlint, the job of the check runs the commands of autofix from .github/checks.toml and keeps the files that they changed. After the checks, the fix bot takes these files as data, only text files that the commit has: on a pull request from a branch of the repository, also one of Renovate, it commits them as one commit onto the branch, and the checks run again; on a pull request from a fork, it suggests them at their lines; on main, it keeps one pull request from bot/self-heal that merges itself. What no command fixes, the PR coach explains.

    failed(["A check fails"])
    command{"A command<br>fixes it?"}
    fix["The job of the check runs the commands of autofix<br>and keeps the files that they changed"]
    bot["The fix bot after the checks<br>takes only text files that the commit has"]
    branch["A branch of this repository, also Renovate's:<br>one commit, and the checks run again"]
    fork["A pull request from a fork:<br>suggestions at their lines"]
    main["main: one pull request from bot/self-heal<br>that merges itself"]
    coach["The PR coach explains<br>what no command fixes"]
    green(["Every check passes"])
    catalog[(".github/checks.toml<br>autofix")]

    failed --> command
    command -- "yes" --> fix --> bot
    command -- "no" --> coach
    bot --> branch
    bot --> fork
    bot --> main
    branch --> green
    main --> green
    fork -- "you commit the suggestions" --> green
    catalog -.-> fix

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class fix,bot,branch,fork,main,coach bot
    class failed person
    class green done
